From ff247080589c1c94d1112698b9cfd73bcc1218f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Date: Sat, 30 Aug 2026 03:23:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] isvp: move SPI NOR env offset to 0x50000

The 320K boot-partition change (U_BOOT_SIZE_KB 256 -> 320) moved the env
partition to 0x50000 everywhere except here. The 2013.07 tree is built via
the LEGACY build system, which ignores configs/uboot/layout/sfcnor.config
entirely -- BR2_TARGET_UBOOT_CONFIG_FRAGMENT_FILES is forced unset by
configs/fragments/uboot/v2013-07.fragment, and Buildroot only consumes that
fragment list under the Kconfig build system. So the fragment bump never
reached this bootloader: it still read and wrote its env at the old 0x40000,
which now lies inside the 320K boot region.

saveenv therefore wrote into the boot partition rather than the env
partition, and env persistence was silently broken (a blank NOR fell back to
the baked-in default env, which is why netconsole settings still appeared to
work). Point the SPI NOR backend at 0x50000 to match the firmware layout.

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
---
 include/configs/isvp_common.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/include/configs/isvp_common.h b/include/configs/isvp_common.h
index b3b5407f..ff247080 100644
--- a/include/configs/isvp_common.h
+++ b/include/configs/isvp_common.h
@@ -613,7 +613,7 @@
 #define CONFIG_ENV_SIZE			(32 << 10)
 #define CONFIG_ENV_OFFSET		(CONFIG_SYS_MONITOR_LEN + CONFIG_SYS_MMCSD_RAW_MODE_U_BOOT_SECTOR * 512)
 #elif defined(CONFIG_ENV_IS_IN_SPI_FLASH)
-#define CONFIG_ENV_OFFSET		0x40000
+#define CONFIG_ENV_OFFSET		0x50000
 #define CONFIG_ENV_SIZE			0x8000
 #define CONFIG_ENV_SECT_SIZE		0x8000
 #else
